        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Maple Leafs are being stripped down and reassembled in real time - and the noise starts with <strong>Mitch Marner 'never protected' by Maple Leafs, agent says</strong>, a line that turns old tension into fresh pressure on the front office. Toronto sits 8th in the Atlantic Division with 78 points, a finished season that has shoved every decision into the spotlight. Brandon Duhaime's arrival has drawn a public nod from Bruce Boudreau, while the Brandon Carlo deal - shipped to St. Louis for two third-round picks - shows this club is still shopping its spine, not polishing the edges. Jack Campbell's warm words about his Maple Leafs years only underline how much the room has changed. <strong>Now comes the real test: whether Toronto can turn cap space and draft capital into a tougher, younger roster before camp opens.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 24, 2026"
