      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Jays are limping, not collapsing - and that's the sliver of light in a season that has spent too much time in the dark. <strong>Shane Bieber's seven sharp innings in Thursday's 3-1 win over the Rays</strong> finally gave Toronto a clean, grown-up performance, and it snapped a four-game skid that had left the club staring at the basement in the AL East. At 47-56, five games back in the division and 12.5 behind, the Blue Jays still look like a club living on the edge of relevance. George Springer and Vladimir Guerrero Jr. each chipped in an RBI, while Louis Varland closed the door in the ninth. <strong>Next comes a Friday night visit to Boston, and Toronto needs Bieber's standard - not a one-off - to keep this patchwork season from unraveling again.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 24, 2026"
      },
