        "body": "The summer has turned the Raptors into a workshop, not a showroom - and that suits a franchise trying to rebuild with purpose. <strong>Toronto's reported interest in Lu Dort says the front office is hunting for a defensive edge, not a headline-grabber.</strong> The club sits 3rd in the Atlantic Division in the final ledger, but that is old paint now; the real work is the roster, the cap sheet, and the draft board. Summer League has already offered a few clues, and the latest chatter around Kawhi Leonard, even on hold, underscores how aggressively Toronto is poking at the market. Kyle Anderson gives them a useful veteran shape, but the next leap has to come from development and fit. <strong>Watch whether the Raptors keep swinging for two-way wings - or settle into a cleaner, younger rotation.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 24, 2026"
